\r\n484:    `SafetyClass`; `scope` and `kind` are left UNDECLARED because a work item\r\n487:    `context_from_need` once the need registry carries them as fields.\"\"\"\r\n521:    \"docs/requirements/hats.toml is absent, or no hat's `applies_when` \"\r\n559:# that is a DEFECT rather than a question — a tag token no hat's `applies_when`\r\n643:    here: work items carry tags too (`context_from_work_item`), so a clause with\r\n650:        for token in context_from_need(need).get(\"tags\", []):\r\n668:        woken_by = \", \".join(_triggers(hat)) or \"(no tag clause) \" + hat[\"applies_when\"]\r\n688:        context = context_from_need(need)\r\n712:        if not any(evaluate(h[\"condition\"], context_from_need(n)) for h in conditional)\r\n730:            1 for n in needs if evaluate(hat[\"condition\"], context_from_need(n))\r\n788:        \"UNKNOWN TAG TOKENS — a tag no hat's `applies_when` can evaluate ({}):\".format(\r\n809:            for t in context_from_need(n).get(\"tags\", [])\r\n826:            _need_id(n) for n in needs if token in context_from_need(n).get(\"tags\", [])\r\n865:# WHY IT IS HERE AND NOT IN trace.py. Applicability needs the `applies_when`\r\n892:PERSPECTIVE_KEYS = (\"applicable\", \"applies_when\", \"produced\", \"no_finding\")\r\n893:DERIVED_KEYS = (\"applicable\", \"applies_when\", \"produced\")\r\n1042:    return [_with_tags(context_from_need(needs[p]), tags) for p in parents]\r\n1047:    `rows`. Each perspective is `{applicable, applies_when, produced}` in roster\r\n1065:            \"applies_when\": hat[\"applies_when\"],\r\n1235:    if args.kind:\r\n1236:        ctx[\"kind\"] = args.kind\r\n1250:                hat[\"name\"], hat[\"applies_when\"], hat[\"asks\"], hat[\"listens_for\"]\r\n1322:    app.add_argument(\"--kind\", default=\"\", help=\"the decomposition's declared kind\")\r\n11:**R1 — The complete sample includes its applicable SR-161 perspective/applicability or no-finding record and respects the required spine boundary.**\n13:**R2 — Each retained child has an independent decision or verification purpose, and the record explains why further splitting stops.**\n17:**B1 — Prose or Hat-Refs is presented as execution of an absent perspective-record producer.**\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
