{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"git show 961f9e47:docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml | Select-String '\"'^'\"\\\\[requirement.SR-161\\\\]' -Context 0,36; git show 961f9e47:docs/requirements/stakeholder-needs.toml | Select-String '\"'^'\"\\\\[need.SN-036\\\\]' -Context 0,24; git rev-parse 90d29557a5986007c16d1a3b2b687bb9dafa0a19:docs/rubrics/plan-decomposition.md\"","aggregated_output":"\r\n> [requirement.SR-161]\r\n  title = \"Decompositions carry a perspective record\"\r\n  sn_refs = [\"SN-036\"]\r\n  boundary_refs = [\"B-05\"]\r\n  hat_refs = [\"TEST-ENGINEER\"]\r\n  requirement = \"\"\"When a decomposition round is reviewed, the delivered planning content shall provide every \r\napplicable declared perspective's question in the decomposition brief and require the sitting's review record to name \r\nthe outcome for each perspective.\"\"\"\r\n  rationale = \"\"\"A decomposition produced from one perspective can look complete while omitting security, operations \r\nor first-use failures. The hats roster and plan briefs already supply the applicable questions, and the sitting's \r\nreview record preserves their outcomes; a separate machine-readable coverage record and checker would duplicate that \r\nreview without improving its adequacy judgment. Hat-Refs remain the row-level provenance for perspectives that raised \r\na requirement. This applies the owner ruling of 2026-09-06 (docs/log.d/2026-09-06-sn036-owner-ruling.md).\"\"\"\r\n  acceptance_criteria = \"\"\"For one completed decomposition round, the applicable perspectives resolve from the \r\ndeclared hats roster, the decomposition brief presents each applicable perspective's question, and the sitting's \r\nreview record names an outcome for every one; the independent adequacy review reads that record.\"\"\"\r\n  priority = \"S\"\r\n  verification = \"Inspection\"\r\n  status = \"Approved\"\r\n  phase = 5\r\n  \r\n  [requirement.SR-162]\r\n  title = \"Requirement boundary references resolve against the declared frame\"\r\n  sn_refs = [\"SN-037\"]\r\n  boundary_refs = [\"B-05\"]\r\n  hat_refs = [\"TEST-ENGINEER\"]\r\n  requirement = \"\"\"The delivered harness shall resolve every system-requirement boundary reference, and every declared \r\ninterface's endpoint pair and signal type, against the declared external frame — an unresolvable crossing failing the \r\nstrict trace naming the row — reporting requirements naming no crossing, crossings named by no requirement, declared \r\ncrossings with no realizing interface row, an interface declaring no endpoint pair or no signal type from the closed \r\ndiscrete/variable vocabulary, and a seam joined to a counterpart whose signal type is incompatible with its own, each \r\nas an advisory, and staying vacuous for a project declaring no frame.\"\"\"\r\n  rationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-037 — every promised behavior's entry and exit locatable at a declared boundary, \r\nunresolved references mechanical findings, in the need's own words. SN-037 had no citing SR even though the machinery \r\nis already delivered (the frame registry, the boundary-reference field, the resolution and coverage rules); this row \r\nis the obligation that machinery enforces. Severity split deliberately: resolution hard, coverage advisory — the ruled \r\nwarn-first sequencing while the corpus converges. The row also carries SN-037's SIGNAL-TYPING half — \"every referenced \r\ninterface identifies its boundary endpoints and whether its signal is discrete or variable ... incompatible signal \r\ntypes are mechanical findings\". That half had ZERO textual occurrence in the SR layer while `orphans=0` held, even \r\nthough `interfaces.toml` already carries a `signal` cell on every row (many of them typed `variable` by a recorded \r\ndefault with a re-type note, which is exactly the state a check is owed for). NAMED RESIDUAL, stated rather than \r\nquietly dropped: the need's last clause — that a reviewed change altering one side of the requirement/interface \r\nrelationship carries or justifies the corresponding change on the other — is a REVIEW obligation this row does not \r\nclaim to mechanize.\"\"\"\r\n  acceptance_criteria = \"\"\"A Boundary-Refs value naming an undeclared crossing joins the --strict failure set naming \r\nthe row; the uncovered-requirement count, the crossings named by no requirement, and the realization gap are each one \r\nadvisory line; an interface row carrying no endpoint pair, or a signal value outside the closed discrete/variable \r\nvocabulary, is reported naming the row; two joined seams whose declared signal types are incompatible are reported \r\nnaming both rows; entity and relationship references in the frame registry resolve; a project declaring no frame is \r\nvacuous.\"\"\"\r\n  priority = \"M\"\r\n  verification = \"Test\"\r\n  status = \"Approved\"\r\n  phase = 5\r\n  \r\n  [requirement.SR-163]\r\n  title = \"Every shipped file maps to a stakeholder outcome\"\r\n  sn_refs = [\"SN-038\"]\r\n  boundary_refs = [\"B-05\"]\r\n  hat_refs = [\"MAINTAINER\"]\r\n  requirement = \"\"\"Every file the delivered package ships shall map, through the declared shipped-file inventory and \r\nits recorded exclusions, to at least one system requirement whose references resolve to a stakeholder need — generated \r\noutputs mapping through their generator — with missing files, stale inventory entries, unresolved references and \r\nunmapped files reported under the declared warning-to-gating policy.\"\"\"\r\n  rationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-038 — a supplied file with no recorded purpose is inherited scope creep, and its absence \r\nof purpose must be a named coverage finding rather than hidden in the tree. SN-038 had no citing SR. The scaffold \r\nMAPPING is the natural declared inventory: it already enumerates what ships, so the coverage universe is a declaration \r\nthat exists rather than a second list that drifts.\"\"\"\r\n  acceptance_criteria = \"\"\"A declared inventory defines the universe and exclusions; a shipped file absent from it, a \r\nstale entry naming a file that no longer ships, an entry whose requirement reference does not resolve to a need, and a \r\nfile with no mapping are each reported; the declared policy assigns warn versus gate per class; a generated output \r\nmaps through its generator's row.\"\"\"\r\n  priority = \"M\"\r\n  verification = \"Test\"\r\n  status = \"Approved\"\r\n> [need.SN-036]\r\n  status = \"Approved\"\r\n  priority = \"S\"\r\n  need = \"\"\"**Scope: template (adopters + this repo).** When a stakeholder's need is turned into detailed \r\nrequirements, it is examined from every relevant expert and downstream-user perspective so important failure cases are \r\nnot lost.\"\"\"\r\n  why = \"\"\"A decomposition produced from one perspective can omit security, operations, accessibility or first-use \r\nfailures while still appearing complete. The omission remains invisible unless the review records which relevant \r\nperspectives were considered and what each contributed.\"\"\"\r\n  acceptance = \"\"\"Each decomposition round is reviewed against every applicable declared perspective, and the review \r\nrecord names each perspective and its outcome. The record demonstrates coverage and provenance; an independent review \r\njudges whether the resulting requirements are adequate.\"\"\"\r\n  \r\n  [need.SN-037]\r\n  status = \"Approved\"\r\n  priority = \"M\"\r\n  need = \"\"\"**Scope: template (adopters + this repo).** A stakeholder can see where each promised system behavior \r\nenters or leaves the system, and the architecture changes with those promises instead of being invented afterward.\"\"\"\r\n  why = \"\"\"A requirement whose inputs and outputs cannot be located at a declared system boundary cannot be verified \r\nor assigned to a responsible component. Updating requirements and architecture separately also leaves periods in which \r\neach tells a different story.\"\"\"\r\n  acceptance = \"\"\"Every system-requirement input and output references a declared interface; every referenced \r\ninterface identifies its boundary endpoints and whether its signal is discrete or variable; every declared \r\ncomponent-boundary crossing has an interface row; unresolved references, uncovered crossings and incompatible signal \r\ntypes are mechanical findings. A reviewed change that alters one side of the requirement/interface relationship must \r\ninclude or explicitly justify the corresponding change on the other side.\"\"\"\r\n  \r\n  [need.SN-038]\r\n  status = \"Approved\"\r\n  tags = [\"templates\"]\r\n  priority = \"M\"\r\n  need = \"\"\"**Scope: template (adopters + this repo).** An adopter can determine why every file supplied by the kit \r\nexists and which stakeholder outcome it supports.\"\"\"\r\n  why = \"\"\"A supplied file with no recorded purpose becomes inherited scope creep: adopters carry, maintain and trust \r\nit even though nobody can explain what failure its removal would cause. The absence must appear as a named coverage \r\nfinding rather than remain hidden in the tree.\"\"\"\r\n  acceptance = \"\"\"A declared shipped-file inventory defines the coverage universe and its exclusions. Every \r\ninventoried file maps to at least one system requirement whose references resolve to a stakeholder need; generated \r\noutputs may map through their generator. A mechanical check reports missing files, stale inventory entries, unresolved \r\nreferences and files with no mapping, and applies the declared warning-to-gating policy.\"\"\"\r\n  \r\n  [need.SN-039]\r\n  status = \"Approved\"\r\n  tags = [\"templates\"]\r\n4f183eb6aa17a459c9b0741391791d03a8f76293\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
